1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,900
Many people read Tao Yuanming

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,700
but the easiest place to misread him

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,166
is treating him as someone who just didn't want to work

4
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:07,733
Picking chrysanthemums by the eastern fence

5
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:09,033
leisurely gazing at the southern mountains

6
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:11,633
sounds too much like an after-work fantasy

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,800
not replying to messages

8
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,800
not checking performance

9
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:14,900
not chasing rankings

10
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:15,966
growing some vegetables

11
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:17,000
drinking a little wine

12
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,300
living your own life

13
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:19,800
So many people say

14
00:00:19,966 --> 00:00:22,133
isn't Tao Yuanming just ancient lying flat

15
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:23,500
I don't think so

16
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:25,100
What's truly powerful about him

17
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,366
isn't escaping work

18
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:28,366
but seeing through a colder question

19
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:30,700
If your living costs are too high

20
00:00:30,766 --> 00:00:32,433
it's hard to be truly free

21
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:34,600
Tao Yuanming didn't simply quit his job

22
00:00:34,766 --> 00:00:37,400
he was actively lowering the fixed costs of his life

23
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,800
This video won't paint him as a saint

24
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,833
or urge you to quit and go back to the countryside tomorrow

25
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:44,200
It just shares one judgment ordinary people can use

26
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:46,733
Freedom isn't doing whatever you want

27
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,633
it's having the power to refuse exchanges not worth it

28
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,833
Picture a scene first

29
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,566
You're sitting in the office

30
00:00:53,766 --> 00:00:55,366
spreadsheets open on your screen

31
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,833
a dozen unread messages on your phone

32
00:00:58,133 --> 00:00:59,233
and your boss suddenly says

33
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,700
could you push a bit tonight

34
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:01,766
You want to say no

35
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,200
but rent is due soon

36
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,366
the credit card needs paying

37
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,766
and family bills pile up

38
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,366
so you swallow the words I don't want to do this

39
00:01:08,433 --> 00:01:11,166
In that moment you lose more than one night

40
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,633
you lose the ability to refuse

41
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:15,133
Tao Yuanming faced a similar question

42
00:01:15,433 --> 00:01:16,600
He served as a minor official

43
00:01:16,766 --> 00:01:18,600
he wasn't completely outside the system

44
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,366
but in the end he chose to leave

45
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,100
Later generations often quote one line

46
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:23,700
not bowing for five pecks of grain

47
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:26,000
This line easily gets retold as aloof pride

48
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:27,500
as if he disdained money

49
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:28,833
But seen from another angle

50
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:31,166
five pecks wasn't about how much money

51
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,833
it represented a kind of exchange

52
00:01:32,966 --> 00:01:34,166
You take a stable income

53
00:01:34,166 --> 00:01:35,100
and trade it for obedience

54
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:35,966
for socializing

55
00:01:35,966 --> 00:01:36,900
for reading moods

56
00:01:36,966 --> 00:01:38,900
for the postures you have to perform every day

57
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:41,533
If this exchange exceeds what you can bear

58
00:01:41,566 --> 00:01:43,400
then income isn't just income anymore

59
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:45,033
it becomes a kind of rent

60
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:47,033
others use it to rent away your time

61
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:48,433
your temper

62
00:01:48,433 --> 00:01:50,166
and a piece of yourself

63
00:01:50,366 --> 00:01:52,200
You may have had this kind of moment too

64
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:53,733
the salary clearly hit your account

65
00:01:53,733 --> 00:01:54,833
but you don't feel relieved

66
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,400
instead you feel renewed for another month

67
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:58,766
This line is a bit harsh

68
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:01,533
but many workers' exhaustion hides right here

69
00:02:01,566 --> 00:02:03,566
It's not that work itself has to be scary

70
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:06,100
it's that you don't know if you still have a choice

71
00:02:06,166 --> 00:02:08,033
The countercultural part of Tao Yuanming is

72
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,533
he wasn't rejecting life

73
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,100
he was retuning life to a price he could afford

74
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,833
What's a fixed cost

75
00:02:15,166 --> 00:02:17,100
it's the money you have to pay

76
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,933
every month whether you're happy or not

77
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:20,133
Rent

78
00:02:20,133 --> 00:02:20,933
mortgage

79
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:21,633
car loan

80
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:22,633
kids' education

81
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:23,766
social face

82
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:24,966
spending habits

83
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,766
the decency others see in you

84
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,800
Once these things pile up

85
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:31,433
your life is like carrying a heavy bag

86
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,933
You can still walk

87
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:35,100
but turning back gets harder with every step

88
00:02:35,433 --> 00:02:37,000
Tao Yuanming returning to the fields

89
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,100
wasn't turning life into a landscape painting

90
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:40,433
He still had to farm

91
00:02:40,433 --> 00:02:41,300
still could be poor

92
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,933
still had uncomfortable moments

93
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:45,400
but he did one crucial thing

94
00:02:45,566 --> 00:02:47,166
he pushed his living costs down

95
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,366
When your meals can be simple

96
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,766
your clothes plain

97
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,233
your socializing reduced

98
00:02:52,366 --> 00:02:54,200
your home not so decent

99
00:02:54,366 --> 00:02:57,333
what you need to exchange with the world becomes less

100
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:58,633
Less exchange

101
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,800
fewer places where you can be squeezed

102
00:03:00,966 --> 00:03:02,566
That's what's powerful about cutting costs

103
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,300
It isn't about making you suffer

104
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,733
it's reducing the buttons others use to control you

105
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:08,600
The hardest part for modern people

106
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,166
isn't failing to understand this

107
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:12,800
it's that living costs got quietly raised

108
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:13,900
You just graduated

109
00:03:13,966 --> 00:03:15,800
thinking a small room is enough

110
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,900
later you want to live more decently

111
00:03:17,966 --> 00:03:19,500
dress more presentably

112
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:21,233
not look too shabby when treating friends

113
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,700
and look good on social media

114
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:26,000
Each one alone isn't too much

115
00:03:26,166 --> 00:03:27,500
but together

116
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:30,300
they keep raising your minimum income

117
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:31,833
Once the minimum rises

118
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:33,700
you can refuse less and less

119
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,933
You say you're chasing a better life

120
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:39,633
but your body's been tied down by a pricier one

121
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,333
A person's most expensive thing

122
00:03:41,566 --> 00:03:43,400
often isn't what they bought

123
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:46,733
but the self they keep paying to maintain it

124
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:49,300
So Tao Yuanming wasn't simply lying flat

125
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:50,833
What is lying flat

126
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:52,166
it's being beaten tired

127
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:53,433
not wanting to move anymore

128
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:55,233
not knowing what's next

129
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,800
Active cost-cutting is different

130
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,333
it's knowing what I want

131
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:02,200
and knowing what isn't worth paying such a high price for

132
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,500
Both look like retreating

133
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,433
but the mindset is completely different

134
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:07,966
One was pushed out

135
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:09,600
the other walked out on their own

136
00:04:09,633 --> 00:04:11,333
You may have seen both kinds of people

137
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:13,100
One says I don't want to grind anymore

138
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,300
but scrolls daily seeing how well others live

139
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,533
the more they scroll the worse they feel

140
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:18,433
the worse they feel the more like a failure

141
00:04:18,533 --> 00:04:20,400
Another kind also cuts consumption

142
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:21,833
skips many gatherings

143
00:04:21,933 --> 00:04:23,433
but they know clearly

144
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:26,566
I am taking back money time and attention

145
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,733
That's the difference

146
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,300
Tao Yuanming's pastoral life

147
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,600
wasn't without cost

148
00:04:30,633 --> 00:04:31,600
It had toil

149
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,500
poverty

150
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,500
and loneliness

151
00:04:33,566 --> 00:04:35,233
But he was willing to pay it

152
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:37,233
because the other side cost more

153
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:39,566
Continuing to bow at a post you don't like

154
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:42,000
maintaining decency in rules you don't believe in

155
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:44,700
pretending to comply in a life that isn't yours

156
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,500
These costs are harder to see

157
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,566
and they hurt more

158
00:04:47,733 --> 00:04:50,200
So he chose a lower-cost version

159
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,300
not the most comfortable

160
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,533
but closer to himself

161
00:04:52,633 --> 00:04:54,200
When we talk about cutting costs today

162
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:56,800
we aren't telling you to live as bitterly as possible

163
00:04:56,933 --> 00:04:58,966
Poverty doesn't automatically bring freedom

164
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:00,833
and roughness isn't the same as clarity

165
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:02,033
What truly needs cutting

166
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:03,766
isn't necessary quality of life

167
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:07,100
but the burdens you keep adding for others to see

168
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,566
You don't need to turn your room into a landscape

169
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:10,933
you only need to ask yourself

170
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,766
are the things I'm working to maintain now

171
00:05:12,966 --> 00:05:14,400
nourishing me

172
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,733
or renting me

173
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,633
Many think fixed cost is only about money

174
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:19,733
it isn't

175
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:21,500
Attention is also a fixed cost

176
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,800
You wake up and scroll through others' lives

177
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:25,566
and your mind starts comparing on its own

178
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,733
That's a cost

179
00:05:26,766 --> 00:05:28,500
Emotion is also a fixed cost

180
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,800
You keep a relationship that drains you

181
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,533
acting out a more decent self every time you meet

182
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:34,800
That's a cost too

183
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:36,600
Identity is also a fixed cost

184
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,233
You tag yourself with cannot-fail

185
00:05:39,333 --> 00:05:41,333
so every choice you can't slow down

186
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:42,166
can't make mistakes

187
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,600
can't admit you're tired

188
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:44,833
That's still a cost

189
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,500
What Tao Yuanming inspires

190
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:48,500
isn't throwing off all responsibility

191
00:05:48,566 --> 00:05:51,566
but putting these invisible costs back on the table

192
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,433
Why am I joining this gathering

193
00:05:53,533 --> 00:05:55,300
why do I have to buy this thing

194
00:05:55,433 --> 00:05:58,366
why must I make others think I'm doing well

195
00:05:58,366 --> 00:05:59,933
Asked enough times

196
00:05:59,966 --> 00:06:01,233
you'll find that much of the pressure

197
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:03,233
wasn't what life originally needed

198
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:05,100
it's what you kept adding

199
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:06,566
to maintain a certain image

200
00:06:06,566 --> 00:06:07,600
Active cost-cutting

201
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,433
means taking those extra images

202
00:06:09,433 --> 00:06:10,800
and peeling them off layer by layer

203
00:06:10,933 --> 00:06:12,433
Not to become shabby

204
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:14,766
but to let yourself be light again

205
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,766
When you're lighter

206
00:06:15,766 --> 00:06:18,166
you can hear where you really want to go

207
00:06:18,433 --> 00:06:21,100
So how can ordinary people use this judgment

208
00:06:21,266 --> 00:06:22,066
First

209
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,833
write out your fixed costs

210
00:06:23,833 --> 00:06:25,566
Don't just write rent and food

211
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:26,933
also write face cost

212
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:28,133
emotional cost

213
00:06:28,166 --> 00:06:29,800
the cost of maintaining personas

214
00:06:29,966 --> 00:06:31,833
Like a circle you don't even like

215
00:06:31,833 --> 00:06:34,200
spending you force yourself into at every gathering

216
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:37,033
things you keep buying to prove you're doing fine

217
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,633
These all charge you rent

218
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:39,400
Second

219
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,600
keep a low-spec life plan for yourself

220
00:06:41,733 --> 00:06:43,733
Not telling you to live bitterly right away

221
00:06:43,733 --> 00:06:44,900
but letting you know

222
00:06:44,933 --> 00:06:46,200
if income drops

223
00:06:46,233 --> 00:06:47,566
if work changes

224
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,233
if you have to rechoose

225
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,900
what's my minimum way to live

226
00:06:50,933 --> 00:06:52,366
The clearer this plan is

227
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,533
the less fear drives you

228
00:06:54,566 --> 00:06:56,033
Many don't dare change paths

229
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,833
not because that path is definitely wrong

230
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,900
but because they've never calculated

231
00:06:59,966 --> 00:07:02,200
how long they could actually last on low cost

232
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,600
A low-spec plan isn't a failure plan

233
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:06,533
it's more like a retreat map

234
00:07:06,633 --> 00:07:08,566
You know what you can stop buying

235
00:07:08,566 --> 00:07:09,800
where you can move

236
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,766
which expenses you can pause

237
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,566
what skills you can trade for money

238
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,900
who you can talk to

239
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,600
Once these are written clearly

240
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,966
fear shrinks

241
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,900
Because fear loves vagueness

242
00:07:19,966 --> 00:07:21,033
The more you avoid looking

243
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:22,300
the more it looks like a mountain

244
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:25,166
Break it into rent food transit medical

245
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,600
and it becomes a list

246
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,900
A list may not look pretty

247
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:29,033
but a list can be changed

248
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,400
A mountain on your back

249
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,900
only makes you gasp for air

250
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,633
This is Tao Yuanming's real value to modern people

251
00:07:34,633 --> 00:07:36,600
He doesn't tell you the distance is always beautiful

252
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,800
he's reminding you

253
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:40,200
when you know how you can minimally live

254
00:07:40,233 --> 00:07:42,166
many things that seem impossible to refuse

255
00:07:42,166 --> 00:07:43,766
suddenly loosen a bit

256
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:45,366
You may not leave right away

257
00:07:45,366 --> 00:07:47,100
but you're not fully scared anymore

258
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,000
This little looseness

259
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,900
is freedom's earliest crack

260
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:50,600
Third

261
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,733
turn freedom from slogan to price

262
00:07:52,766 --> 00:07:54,333
You want no overtime on weekends

263
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:55,233
it has a price

264
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:57,233
You want less useless socializing

265
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,166
it has a price

266
00:07:58,166 --> 00:08:00,200
You want opportunities without pleasing

267
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,366
it also has a price

268
00:08:01,366 --> 00:08:03,400
This price might be buying less

269
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,533
comparing less

270
00:08:04,533 --> 00:08:06,200
chasing less surface decency

271
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:09,100
or admitting you don't fit certain scenes

272
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:11,433
admitting you don't want certain dinners

273
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:14,300
admitting you don't have the energy to please everyone

274
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,600
These are small things

275
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,900
but each admission

276
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,900
means one less invisible rent paid

277
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:20,200
Many stay tired

278
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,233
not because there's too much to handle

279
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:25,433
but because they want to keep looking good at everything

280
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:27,000
Looking good is too expensive

281
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,966
It makes you when already tired

282
00:08:29,033 --> 00:08:31,033
spend energy performing that you're not

283
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:32,300
The first step of cutting costs

284
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:34,766
is letting your life not look so good

285
00:08:34,766 --> 00:08:36,166
but be more real

286
00:08:36,166 --> 00:08:37,566
A more real life

287
00:08:37,566 --> 00:08:38,900
has the chance to get lighter

288
00:08:38,966 --> 00:08:40,133
It doesn't sound romantic

289
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:41,400
but it's very real

290
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,566
Freedom isn't a gift that suddenly arrives

291
00:08:43,566 --> 00:08:46,033
it's a space you buy back bit by bit

292
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,633
The best part of Tao Yuanming

293
00:08:47,633 --> 00:08:49,833
isn't giving us a dream of escaping the world

294
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:51,100
but reminding us

295
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,100
that much pressure isn't given by fate

296
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:56,633
it's bills we signed to maintain a pricier self

297
00:08:56,733 --> 00:08:58,633
When you tune life lighter

298
00:08:58,633 --> 00:09:00,200
you may not be happy at once

299
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,200
but you'll have a little more room to refuse

300
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,833
a little more space to breathe

301
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:06,533
a little more confidence to keep walking without explaining

302
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:08,800
The most moving part of picking chrysanthemums by the eastern fence

303
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:09,800
isn't the chrysanthemums

304
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:10,900
or the southern mountains

305
00:09:10,933 --> 00:09:11,933
but that moment

306
00:09:11,966 --> 00:09:15,700
he finally didn't have to bend himself into someone others liked for a few pecks of grain

307
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:18,966
In the next video we'll keep using an everyday object

308
00:09:18,966 --> 00:09:20,633
to explain a social rule

309
00:09:20,633 --> 00:09:22,933
Because many things that truly shape life

310
00:09:22,966 --> 00:09:26,733
hide inside what you see every day but never really looked at

311
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:27,566
See you next time

